course: dictionary
lesson: 14162
title: Misunderstood
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Misunderstood is the past form of misunderstand. It means understood wrongly. «I wanted to help, but my sister misunderstood me and got cross.» My sister understood my words the wrong way, so she was cross.
explain: A misunderstood person or thing is one that people judge wrongly, or do not really understand. «The giant was lonely, but everyone thought he was scary. He was misunderstood.» The clues are lonely and everyone thought he was scary: people got him wrong, but he was not really bad.
explain: Look for the little word mis-, which means wrong or badly, as in mistake and mislead. Try swapping in "understood wrongly" for misunderstood. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Misunderstand means to understand wrongly.
fact: Misunderstood is the past form of misunderstand, and it can also be used as an adjective to describe a person or thing.
fact: «Misunderstood» can describe a person or thing that people judge wrongly.
fact: In stories, a misunderstood character is often not bad; others just do not understand them.
fact: Sharks, bats and spiders are often called misunderstood animals, because people fear them more than they should.
exercise: «I did not mean to be rude, but Ben misunderstood what I said.» What does misunderstood mean here? | Forgot it completely | Heard it twice | Understood perfectly | *Understood wrongly
exercise: «The wolf in the story was misunderstood, not wicked.» What does this tell us? | The story was never written | The wolf was very clever | The wolf was wicked after all | *People judged the wolf wrongly
exercise: Which word means understood wrongly? | *misunderstood | underline | undertake | understood
test: «Sharks are often called misunderstood animals.» What does this mean? | Sharks live on land | *People judge sharks wrongly and fear them more than they should | Sharks can talk to people | Sharks are very slow swimmers
test: Priya says, «My brother misunderstood the plan and went to the wrong park.» Why did he go to the wrong park? | He never heard about the plan | He wanted a longer walk | *He understood the plan wrongly | He lost his bike on the way
exam: «The lonely giant was misunderstood by the village, but he was kind.» What does misunderstood tell us about the giant? | He was the village leader | *The village judged him wrongly | He could not walk | The village loved him very much
